# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository regardless of checkout OS.
#
# This matters more here than in most repos: `ai-rulez verify --plugin` compares
# content hashes of the generated trees (skills/, commands/, .claude-plugin/)
# against their .ai-rulez/ sources. A CRLF round-trip through a Windows checkout
# changes those bytes and fails the check with an error that says nothing about
# line endings. CI already runs a Windows job, so the exposure is real.
#
# No *.ps1 / *.cmd carve-out yet — this repo ships no Windows scripts. Add
# `*.ps1 text eol=crlf` when it does (see the SessionStart hook discussion).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated payloads. Marking them collapses them in GitHub diffs and excludes
# them from language stats, so a review shows the .ai-rulez/ source change
# rather than the same edit repeated across every host package.
# Edit .ai-rulez/ — never these.
# These four patterns cover exactly the 28 paths in .ai-rulez-generated.json
# (21 + 4 + 2 + 1). The manifest itself is generated too, but cannot list itself.
skills/**                linguist-generated=true
commands/**              linguist-generated=true
.claude-plugin/**        linguist-generated=true
.codex-plugin/**         linguist-generated=true
.ai-rulez-generated.json linguist-generated=true

# NOT marked: .agents/plugins/marketplace.json and plugin.json are hand-authored
# adapters (ai-rulez does not generate the Codex marketplace or the Antigravity
# manifest), so their diffs must stay visible.
